# .gitignore — WNBA Analytics
# Added in Phase 4 for security/technical-review finding L-5.
#
# IMPORTANT (read before assuming this file is doing its job): a .gitignore only
# affects UNTRACKED paths. Phase 0's `git init` baseline commit captured
# `.Rhistory`, `logs/logs.duckdb`, `logs/analytics.duckdb` and
# `logs/wnba_pipeline.log` as tracked files, so the rules below will NOT take
# effect for them until someone runs, once, from the repo root:
#
#     git rm --cached .Rhistory logs/logs.duckdb logs/analytics.duckdb logs/wnba_pipeline.log
#
# That is an index operation and is deliberately left to the orchestrator rather
# than performed by the agent that wrote this file. Everything else here is
# purely forward-looking.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R session state — the L-5 finding proper.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .Rhistory is a verbatim transcript of past interactive sessions. Today's copy
# holds no secret (it captured fetch_market_odds() including the
# Sys.getenv("ODDS_API_KEY", "") block, which is the safe pattern), but any
# future session in which a human pastes a live key would record it here. This
# repo's standing rule is that no secret is ever committed; keeping session
# transcripts out of version control is the cheap structural enforcement of it.
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# Never commit a real credential file. All keys/webhooks are read via
# Sys.getenv(..., "") — .Renviron is where a human would actually set them.
.Renviron
.Renviron.local
.env

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime logs — pure diff noise.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# logging_utils.R appends a real row to logs/wnba_pipeline.log and logs/logs.duckdb
# on every pipeline run AND every test run, so these show as modified in `git
# status` after any verification work, with no source change behind it (flagged
# by agent_foundation in its Wave 1 handoff). logs_pending_<pid>.tsv is the M-7
# spill file written when the DuckDB handle is held by another process.
logs/*.duckdb
logs/*.duckdb.wal
logs/*.log
logs/logs_pending_*.tsv
pipeline_execution.log

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch scripts.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md mandates writing R code to a temp .R file rather than using inline
# multi-line `Rscript -e` (which segfaults on this machine), so throwaway scripts
# are a structural, recurring by-product of doing any work here. L-5 was exactly
# these accumulating at repo root, where the convention is that every root .R is
# a pipeline script sourced by bare filename. Genuine one-off utilities belong in
# tools/ with a descriptive name (see tools/derive_props_distribution_params.R,
# which absorbed the four deleted temp_derive_*/temp_check_* files).
temp_*.R
temp_*.r
_tmp_*.R
_tmp_*.r
.tmp_*.R
.tmp_*.r

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor noise.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, on purpose: cache/ and data/.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These hold generated .rds/.csv artifacts, but they are tracked deliberately —
# the dashboard, the props engines and the health probe all read them, several
# are slow to regenerate (RAPM over 292k possessions, the LOSO benchmarks), and
# Phase 4's Wave 3 cache-invalidation task depends on having their prior state in
# git to diff against. Do not add cache/ or data/ here.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Misc R/RStudio artifacts (merged in from a GitHub-generated template that
# briefly conflicted with this file — see git history; /cache/ and docs/ were
# deliberately dropped from that template, per the section above).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.RDataTmp
.Ruserdata
*-Ex.R
/*.tar.gz
/*.Rcheck/
vignettes/*.html
vignettes/*.pdf
.httr-oauth
*_cache/
*.utf8.md
*.knit.md
po/*~
rsconnect/
